{
  "requirement": "The mdBook preprocessor MUST report an error when a generated evidence detail page would use the path of an existing book chapter.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation.** `DetailPlan::find` in `src/index.rs` carries `{impl}` markers for `requirements.index.path_conflicts`. One is on the function and one is on the conflict-check block.\n- It computes each generated detail path with `detail_path`.\n- It collects the paths of all existing book chapters, `book.chapters().filter_map(|c| c.path)`, into `existing_paths`.\n- It returns `InvalidData` with the message \"generated evidence page … conflicts with a book chapter\" if any generated path is already in `existing_paths`.\n- `src/lib.rs` calls `DetailPlan::find` with `?`, so the error propagates out of the preprocessor. That meets the \"MUST report an error\" obligation.\n\n**Test.** `generated_detail_path_cannot_replace_a_chapter` has a `{test}` marker for the requirement.\n- It builds a book with an index chapter and an existing chapter at `requirements/requirements.ready.md`.\n- It defines `requirements.ready` in `requirements.md`, so the generated path is `requirements/requirements.ready.md`.\n- It asserts that `find` fails with \"conflicts with a book chapter\".\n\nThe test covers the one scenario the requirement describes: a nested path collision with an existing chapter. The non-colliding path is exercised by the other index tests that populate pages successfully.\n\n**Minor observation.** The same check also rejects two generated pages that share a path (`!generated.insert(path)`). The requirement does not mention this. It looks unreachable in practice, because definition names are unique map keys and each chapter has its own directory. It reports the same kind of path-collision error, so I treat it as defensive and not a real gap.\n\nNo other uncited code implements this requirement.",
  "inputs": [
    {
      "requirements": "requirements.index.path_conflicts",
      "matches": [
        "requirements.index.path_conflicts"
      ],
      "text": [
        ":::{req} path_conflicts",
        "The mdBook preprocessor MUST report an error when a generated evidence detail page would use the path of an existing book chapter.",
        ":::"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/index.rs",
      "rust_item": "impl[DetailPlan]/fn[find]",
      "text": [
        "    // {impl}`requirements.index.chapter`",
        "    // {impl}`requirements.examples.index`",
        "    // {impl}`requirements.index.detail_pages`",
        "    // {impl}`requirements.index.path_conflicts`",
        "    pub(crate) fn find(",
        "        book: &Book,",
        "        definitions: &BTreeMap<String, Definition>,",
        "        order: &[String],",
        "    ) -> io::Result<Self> {",
        "        let mut index_path = None;",
        "        for chapter in book.chapters() {",
        "            for _ in marker_ranges(&chapter.content)? {",
        "                if index_path.is_some() {",
        "                    return Err(invalid_index(",
        "                        \"a book may contain only one {requirements-index} directive\",",
        "                    ));",
        "                }",
        "                index_path = chapter.path.clone();",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "        let mut detail_paths = BTreeMap::new();",
        "        let mut chapters: Vec<(PathBuf, Vec<String>)> = Vec::new();",
        "        for name in order {",
        "            let Some(definition) = definitions.get(name) else {",
        "                continue;",
        "            };",
        "            let path = detail_path(&definition.path, name);",
        "            detail_paths.insert(name.clone(), path);",
        "            match chapters",
        "                .iter_mut()",
        "                .find(|(chapter, _)| *chapter == definition.path)",
        "            {",
        "                Some((_, names)) => names.push(name.clone()),",
        "                None => chapters.push((definition.path.clone(), vec![name.clone()])),",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "        let existing_paths = book",
        "            .chapters()",
        "            .filter_map(|chapter| chapter.path.as_ref())",
        "            .collect::<BTreeSet<_>>();",
        "        // {impl}`requirements.index.path_conflicts`",
        "        let mut generated = BTreeSet::new();",
        "        for path in detail_paths.values() {",
        "            if existing_paths.contains(path) || !generated.insert(path) {",
        "                return Err(invalid_index(&format!(",
        "                    \"generated evidence page {} conflicts with a book chapter\",",
        "                    path.display()",
        "                )));",
        "            }",
        "        }",
        "        Ok(Self {",
        "            index_path,",
        "            detail_paths,",
        "            chapters,",
        "        })",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
    {
      "rust_file": "src/index.rs",
      "rust_item": "mod[tests]/fn[generated_detail_path_cannot_replace_a_chapter]",
      "text": [
        "    // {test}`requirements.index.path_conflicts`",
        "    #[test]",
        "    fn generated_detail_path_cannot_replace_a_chapter() {",
        "        let mut book = Book::new();",
        "        book.push_item(Chapter::new(",
        "            \"Index\",",
        "            \":::{requirements-index}\\n:::\\n\".to_owned(),",
        "            \"requirements-index.md\",",
        "            Vec::new(),",
        "        ));",
        "        book.push_item(Chapter::new(",
        "            \"Existing\",",
        "            String::new(),",
        "            \"requirements/requirements.ready.md\",",
        "            Vec::new(),",
        "        ));",
        "        let definitions = BTreeMap::from([(",
        "            \"requirements.ready\".to_owned(),",
        "            Definition {",
        "                path: Path::new(\"requirements.md\").to_path_buf(),",
        "                text: \"Ready MUST work.\".to_owned(),",
        "                kind: DefinitionKind::Requirement,",
        "            },",
        "        )]);",
        "        let error = match DetailPlan::find(&book, &definitions, &[\"requirements.ready\".to_owned()])",
        "        {",
        "            Err(error) => error,",
        "            Ok(_) => panic!(\"a generated detail page replaced a chapter\"),",
        "        };",
        "        assert!(error.to_string().contains(\"conflicts with a book chapter\"));",
        "    }"
      ]
    },
